 "relevance_note": "Case 1 describes a woman with Tangier disease and her sister, both homozygous for an ABCA1 splice variant: \"Her sister was homozygote for the same sequence variation\".",
 "method_note": "Hand extraction, JSON assembled by a short script; spans checked verbatim by script. Scope: only Case 1 (Tangier disease, ABCA1) and her sister are in scope; Case 2 (LCAT) and Case 3 (APOA1) patients get no rows and are counted in cohort_size_as_stated = 3. Label 'Case 1' taken from the section heading; the sister has no own label. Table 1 has patients as columns; the 'ABCA1' column header is the Case 1 patient (text: 'the patient's lipid profile has been consistently abnormal (Table 1)'); its values are ranges, not stacked cells. Apolipoprotein A1 cell is empty for ABCA1, so low apoA-I is not reported. Hypertriglyceridemia recorded from the Table 1 value 217–295 against the printed normal range 30–150, not from a textual statement. Pronoun attribution: the paragraph starting 'Her sibling had a milder form of the disease' continues with 'she' (peripheral neuropathy, CVA, childhood tonsillectomy, orange colonic mucosa); these were attributed to the sister, consistent with 'Of note, her sister had a CVA episode later on during follow up', but the pronouns are ambiguous. Syringomyelia-like syndrome in Case 1 was not mapped to the peripheral neuropathy checklist item (not stated as neuropathy for her). Recurrent strokes and the MRI emboli (Figure 1B) are not stated as atherosclerotic, so the non-coronary atherosclerotic item is not reported; Figure 1B is not clearly attributed to a person and was not used. Orange colonic mucosa was not mapped to 'intestinal mucosal lipid deposits' (no lipid deposits stated). Consanguinity is stated for the Case 1 woman only and was not copied to the sister. Age at diagnosis: only the year 1997 is given, so not reported. Contradictions noted: text says 'abnormally low' total cholesterol while Table 1 gives 85–102 against a normal range of 80–200; Figure 1A legend says 'Lane 1 is control, and the two Tangier Diseased sisters in Lanes #1 & #2'; the Summary says 'three patients with mutations in CETP, LCAT, and ABCA1' whereas the cases are ABCA1, LCAT and APOA1; Figure 1D calls the LCAT missense change a 'homozygous splice site error' (out of scope). The genomic coordinate is printed without a genome build.",
